\newcommand{\conventions}{\paragraph{Conventions.} Rational means complete and transitive. Continuity means a closed weak-preference graph: if $x^n\to x$, $y^n\to y$ and $x^n\pref y^n$ for all $n$, then $x\pref y$. Convex preferences have convex upper contour sets. Strict convexity uses distinct bundles and mixtures with weights in $(0,1)$. Monotonicity means $x\gg y\Rightarrow x\spref y$; strong monotonicity means $x\ge y$, $x\ne y\Rightarrow x\spref y$. Local nonsatiation (LNS) means every relative neighbourhood of every bundle contains a strictly preferred bundle. All topological statements use the stated domain's relative Euclidean topology.}
